{"title":"How We Think","story":[{"type":"paragraph","id":"efa815b2689ab49c","text":"How We Think: A Restatement of the Relation of Reflective Thinking to the Educative Process is a 1933 classic book by American philosopher and educator John Dewey. It revises his 1910 work to argue that schools must teach students how to think critically and scientifically through active, experiential problem-solving rather than rote memorization."},{"type":"paragraph","id":"bdaf62ad2afb0c8f","text":"As per Dewey, thinking or reflective thinking is — “an active, persistent, and careful assessment of a belief or supposed form of knowledge, the reasons for that knowledge, and the additional conclusions to which knowledge leads.”"},{"type":"paragraph","id":"8b374af5ce2a9a1f","text":"[https://thethinkinglane.medium.com/deweys-five-steps-of-reflective-thinking-b81fb6326a6a source]"},{"type":"paragraph","id":"aab4667a58afd63d","text":"[https://archive.org/details/howwethinkrestat00dewerich/page/30/mode/2up ebook]"},{"type":"pagefold","id":"e2a9ae9ed46796db","text":"related"},{"type":"paragraph","id":"dd58398f2e473674","text":"[[John Dewey]]"},{"type":"paragraph","id":"217b0067e707e17c","text":"[[Reflective Practice]]"}],"journal":[{"type":"create","item":{"title":"How We Think","story":[]},"date":1788470423721},{"type":"fork","date":1788470436159},{"item":{"type":"factory","id":"efa815b2689ab49c"},"id":"efa815b2689ab49c","type":"add","date":1788470438677},{"type":"edit","id":"efa815b2689ab49c","item":{"type":"paragraph","id":"efa815b2689ab49c","text":"How We Think: A Restatement of the Relation of Reflective Thinking to the Educative Process is a 1933 classic book by American philosopher and educator John Dewey. It revises his 1910 work to argue that schools must teach students how to think critically and scientifically through active, experiential problem-solving rather than rote memorization."},"date":1788470441809},{"item":{"type":"factory","id":"aab4667a58afd63d"},"id":"aab4667a58afd6